---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Cookie Policy"
  description="Which cookies I-Field sets, what they do, and how to change your choice at any time."
  updated="2026-08-10"
>
  <p class="lead">
    This site sets as little as possible. Nothing that tracks you runs unless you have
    actively allowed it.
  </p>

  <h2>Strictly necessary</h2>
  <p>
    We store your cookie choice in your browser's local storage so we do not have to ask on
    every visit. It contains only your decision and the date you made it. No third party can
    read it, and it is not used to identify you.
  </p>

  <h2>Analytics</h2>
  <p>
    If you allow analytics, we load Google Analytics 4 to count visits and see which pages
    people find useful. It sets first-party cookies, typically <code>_ga</code> and
    <code>_ga_&lt;id&gt;</code>, which distinguish one browser from another so repeat visits
    are not double-counted. IP addresses are anonymised.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>If you decline, nothing is loaded at all</strong> — no request is made to Google,
    and no analytics cookie is created. If you allow analytics and later change your mind,
    we stop collecting and delete those cookies from your browser.
  </p>

  <h2>Advertising</h2>
  <p>
    None. This site runs no advertising or remarketing tags, and the corresponding consent
    signals are permanently set to denied.
  </p>

  <h2>Changing your mind</h2>
  <p>
    You can change your choice whenever you like.
  </p>
  <p>
    <button type="button" class="chip" data-cc-action="preferences">
      Open cookie preferences
    </button>
  </p>
  <p>
    Clearing your browser's storage for this site also resets the choice, and you will be
    asked again on your next visit.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
